    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255-a10">

                <pb facs="0531" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg525"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 10 in No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Affidavit of Mr. Wilson.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Honolulu, Oahu</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hawaiian Islands, ss:</hi></p>
                <p>And now comes Charles B. Wilson, of Honolulu aforesaid, and upon oath deposes and
                    says:</p>
                <p>That on the 17th day of January, A. D. 1893, between 3:30 and 4 p.m., of that
                    day, while he was in charge of the police station as marshal of the Kingdom, he
                    saw and read a letter from the American Minister Stevens addressed to Her
                    Majesty’s ministers, wherein Minister Stevens stated that he had recognized the
                    Provisional Government as the de facto Government of the Hawaiian Islands.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. B. Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Subscribed and sworn to before me this 4th day of May, A. D. 1893.</p>
                    <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>]<signed><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">F. J. Testa</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Notary Public, First Judicial
                            Circuit.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
